<title>USA: Kansas feedlot cattle markets quiet - USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas feedlot cattle markets quiet - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade quiet. No sales slaughter steers or heifers confirmed. Inquiry and demand moderate.</p>
<p>Cattle priced at $71.00-$72.00, bids $68.00-$69.00, last established prices were 69.00 on Thursday.</p>
<p>Week-to-date 3600 head confirmed, mostly all previously contracted or formulated cattle.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
